1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,036
This is the synthetic card dispute workbench from team bob the builder, for Track Three, Reasoning Architecture.

2
00:00:07,036 --> 00:00:10,761
Two separately invoked agents investigate and challenge a proposal.

3
00:00:10,761 --> 00:00:12,831
Deterministic code protects every action.

4
00:00:12,831 --> 00:00:15,728
All records and financial effects are fictional.

5
00:00:15,728 --> 00:00:19,867
This edited walkthrough uses actual application captures and dated evidence.

6
00:00:20,267 --> 00:00:23,886
A dispute analyst needs more than a plausible answer.

7
00:00:23,886 --> 00:00:30,321
The application checks source evidence, existing refunds and the policy that applied when the case opened.

8
00:00:30,321 --> 00:00:33,941
The workbench separates the recommendation from what actually persisted.

9
00:00:33,941 --> 00:00:38,767
Ordinary outcomes run automatically, while policy exceptions enter a saved review queue.

10
00:00:39,167 --> 00:00:41,176
Zetaris supplies a fresh snapshot.

11
00:00:41,176 --> 00:00:43,990
The Investigator proposes an outcome through Nightshift.

12
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:50,019
A deterministic critic checks policy and citations before a separate Nightshift Reviewer challenges the evidence.

13
00:00:50,019 --> 00:00:53,234
One correction token is shared across both checks.

14
00:00:53,234 --> 00:01:00,067
Both must accept the same final proposal before the restricted writer rechecks the source and commits atomically.

15
00:01:00,467 --> 00:01:04,818
Here we selected case D P twenty nine in the actual live workbench.

16
00:01:04,818 --> 00:01:09,840
The case has a one hundred and thirty Singapore dollar claim under policy version one.

17
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:10,844
We clicked Investigate.

18
00:01:10,844 --> 00:01:16,200
The running state reports no effect while the controller obtains source facts and calls the agents.

19
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:19,163
In this real run the Reviewer objected.

20
00:01:19,163 --> 00:01:23,923
The Investigator revised once, the critic accepted again, and the Reviewer objected again.

21
00:01:23,923 --> 00:01:26,485
Four live calls ended without a write.

22
00:01:26,485 --> 00:01:31,611
The objection appears overly conservative because the filing window already selected a terminal outcome.

23
00:01:31,611 --> 00:01:33,076
We preserve that refusal.

24
00:01:33,076 --> 00:01:39,300
The second agent can block an action, but cannot change policy or invent a review queue entry.

25
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:44,173
For case D P twenty, the Investigator requested missing refund confirmation.

26
00:01:44,173 --> 00:01:48,647
The critic accepted, and the independent Reviewer accepted the same proposal.

27
00:01:48,647 --> 00:01:54,340
The final gate passed and PostgreSQL committed the evidence request, with zero credit effect.

28
00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:56,780
This used two real Nightshift calls.

29
00:01:56,780 --> 00:02:02,067
Exact saved request recovery later reused the same decision with no model calls.

30
00:02:02,467 --> 00:02:05,621
This separate rehearsal deliberately scripts a Reviewer objection.

31
00:02:05,621 --> 00:02:13,508
The Investigator revises with a new proposal identity, the critic checks again, and the Reviewer accepts before the guarded write.

32
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:19,424
These are scripted model responses with real isolated PostgreSQL and the pinned H MEM reference.

33
00:02:19,424 --> 00:02:25,733
Two fresh cycles each produced eight decisions, four credits and one review, covering all four outcomes.

34
00:02:26,133 --> 00:02:32,375
Two hundred and ninety eight application tests and sixteen reference checks passed with no skips.

35
00:02:32,375 --> 00:02:36,120
A fresh clone reproduced the rehearsal without private configuration.

36
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:40,280
Both live roles returned the Nemotron model label shown here.

37
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:43,609
That is response metadata, not independent provider attestation.

38
00:02:43,609 --> 00:02:47,770
H MEM remains source verified and advisory, with mock embeddings.

39
00:02:47,770 --> 00:02:50,267
These live demonstrations explicitly disabled memory.

40
00:02:50,667 --> 00:02:57,275
The implementation still uses synthetic document templates, one PostgreSQL datasource and no universal semantic layer.

41
00:02:57,275 --> 00:03:03,883
The deck, video, transcript and dated traces preserve these limits and the earlier fallback package.

42
00:03:03,883 --> 00:03:09,170
Distinct live agent roles are demonstrated, but organizer acceptance is not claimed.

43
00:03:09,170 --> 00:03:17,100
The team leader still must verify playable hosting, contributor declarations, the portal form and the final submission receipt.
